---
import { Code } from '@astrojs/starlight/components';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import overwhelmed from '../assets/beaver-holding-stack-of-papers.png';

// The example from the README, verbatim: the same issue the quick start walks
// through, after it has been started, noted, and closed.
const file = `---
id: ix2guj
title: Login form rejects valid passwords
state: done
assignee: stefan
priority: high
labels:
  - bug
created: 2026-07-06T20:28:40Z
updated: 2026-07-06T20:28:59Z
---

When a user submits a correct password containing a \`!\`, the form clears and
shows "invalid credentials". Expected: the login succeeds.

## Notes

**stefan** — 2026-07-06T20:28:59Z

root cause: form strips ! before hashing
`;
---

<section class="landing-section not-content">
	<div class="split">
		<div class="text">
			<h2 class="landing-heading">One file per issue. The file is the record.</h2>
			<div class="landing-body">
				<p>
					Each issue is one file in <code>.beaver/issues/</code>, named
					<code>&lt;id&gt;-&lt;slug&gt;.md</code>. The short random ID is the identity; the
					slug just mirrors the title.
				</p>
				<p>
					The frontmatter is machine-owned: Beaver Backlog keeps it formatted, and unknown
					keys you add by hand are preserved verbatim. The body is yours; the tool only ever
					appends notes to it.
				</p>
				<p>
					State is one of <code>todo</code>, <code>in-progress</code>, <code>done</code>, or
					<code>cancelled</code>. Any state may move to any other: the tracker records reality
					rather than enforcing a workflow.
				</p>
				<p>
					<a class="landing-link" href="/issue-file/">Read the file format</a>
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
		<div class="landing-code code">
			<Code lang="markdown" title="ix2guj-login-form-rejects-valid-passwords.md" code={file} wrap />
			<Image
				src={overwhelmed}
				widths={[320, 640]}
				sizes="15rem"
				width={640}
				alt="The beaver struggling under a tower of loose paper"
				loading="lazy"
				class="landing-art is-bottom-right"
				style="--tilt: 8deg; --art-width: 15rem; --art-over-x: 6rem; --art-over-y: 4.5rem;"
			/>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

